No third-party source is included here. The build, the examples and the demos use the
material below, each fetched from its own project and staying under its own licence.

1. Apache Flink, under the Apache License, Version 2.0

   https://flink.apache.org. This project implements an SPI that Flink discovers through
   ServiceLoader. Flink is a `provided` dependency: it is compiled against and expected on
   the TaskManager, and no Flink class is redistributed here.

   The SPI is not in any Flink release. It exists on branch `gpu-offload` of
   https://github.com/beestream-ai/flink, a fork of https://github.com/apache/flink, and
   those changes stay under the Apache Software Foundation's Apache 2.0 licence and keep its
   file headers. Nothing here relicenses them.

2. TornadoVM, under the Apache License, Version 2.0

   https://github.com/beehive-lab/TornadoVM, used in two ways and redistributed in neither:
   as the Maven artifacts io.github.beehive-lab:tornado-api, :tornado-cublas and
   :tornado-cudf, all `provided`; and at run time as an installed SDK with the CUDA backend,
   which the TaskManager loads from its own module path.

3. NVIDIA RAPIDS libcudf, under the Apache License, Version 2.0

   https://github.com/rapidsai/cudf. Reached only through TornadoVM's cuDF binding, never
   linked or called directly from this project, and not redistributed. It is expected on
   LD_LIBRARY_PATH at run time; where it is absent the operators that use it decline and the
   query runs on the host.

4. The NVIDIA CUDA toolkit and cuBLAS, under the NVIDIA Software Licence Agreement

   https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-toolkit. TornadoVM's cuBLAS binding dlopens the system
   library through java.lang.foreign. Nothing of NVIDIA's is bundled, compiled or
   redistributed here.

5. jitllm, under the Apache License, Version 2.0

   https://github.com/beestream-ai/jitllm, a `provided` dependency of the examples module
   only. The LLM pipeline example runs inference in the TaskManager's own JVM through it;
   nothing in the provider itself refers to it.

6. llama.cpp, under the MIT Licence

   https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp. The demo scripts build it from source, on the
   reader's machine, as the CPU baseline the LLM pipeline example is compared against. No
   source or binary of it is included here.

7. Model weights and data sets

   The demos download model weights and generate or fetch their own data sets. Each stays
   under the licence its publisher states; none is redistributed in this repository.
